+# Closed Café — Location Design
+
+**Target specification; existing playable content is unchanged.**
+
+## Purpose and geography
+
+Compare the radio signal with Elian’s original cassette.
+
+Arrival from visitor-centre; departure to market-street. Reuse the current authored environment and entry/exit identities. New controls occupy reachable close-inspection views rather than requiring new locomotion.
+
+## First readable situation
+
+The cassette waveform has one gull peak followed by two bell peaks.
+
+## Authored interaction zones
+
+- Zone 1: **Tune the Witness Transmission**. Find the broadcast that matches Elian’s original cassette. Controls: cassette, radio-dial, compare-switch. A wide view must expose its location before a close view is required.
+- Zone 2: **Open the Service Hatch**. Open a quiet route toward the market. Controls: tray, counter-hook, upper-latch. A wide view must expose its location before a close view is required.
+- Zone 3: **Test the Kitchen Voice**. Document the source of the imitated voice. Controls: threshold-view, recorder-switch, cable. A wide view must expose its location before a close view is required.
+
+## Spatial constraints
+
+Keep the exit and named shelter visible from the primary interaction zone. No required control may sit behind a permanently locked optional object. Reused return environments keep their landmark positions; state variants change lighting and access, not the meaning of established navigation symbols. Initial blockout uses labelled zones; final dimensions and camera framing need a measured asset/layout review.
+
+## Existing atmosphere to retain
+
+Two cups stand beneath a dead wall clock. One holds a skin of milk; the other is dry. From the kitchen, Elian asks you to come closer. On your cassette she warned you about a voice that knows names. You put the tape on the counter before answering anything.
+
+This paragraph is archival narrative context, not a required arrival popup in the target design. Deliver its essential facts through the encounter actions; retain full writing in the optional journal.
+
+## Existing safe retreat
+
+You step outside the service door. The kitchen voice keeps talking to an empty café.
+
+## Encounter specifications
+
+- [CF-01 — Tune the Witness Transmission](tune-the-witness-transmission.md) — puzzle; required.
+- [CF-02 — Open the Service Hatch](open-the-service-hatch.md) — puzzle; required.
+- [CF-03 — Test the Kitchen Voice](test-the-kitchen-voice.md) — investigation; optional.
