+# Parish House — Location Design
+
+**Target specification; existing playable content is unchanged.**
+
+## Purpose and geography
+
+Recover the relay contract and the descent equipment.
+
+Arrival from chapel-nave; departure to maintenance-tunnels. Reuse the current authored environment and entry/exit identities. New controls occupy reachable close-inspection views rather than requiring new locomotion.
+
+## First readable situation
+
+Three dated photographs show four bricked window panels, alcove one and seven bell bands.
+
+## Authored interaction zones
+
+- Zone 1: **Open the Mechanical Safe**. Recover the relay contract from physical evidence in the room. Controls: photograph-slider, number-wheel, safe-handle. A wide view must expose its location before a close view is required.
+- Zone 2: **Expose the Descent Entrance**. Find the utility stair and prepare a return route. Controls: cabinet-catch, survey-board, chalk, letter-view. A wide view must expose its location before a close view is required.
+- Zone 3: **Examine the Hidden Photograph**. Give the family discovery a personal response. Controls: photo-flap, conversation, journal. A wide view must expose its location before a close view is required.
+
+## Spatial constraints
+
+Keep the exit and named shelter visible from the primary interaction zone. No required control may sit behind a permanently locked optional object. Reused return environments keep their landmark positions; state variants change lighting and access, not the meaning of established navigation symbols. Initial blockout uses labelled zones; final dimensions and camera framing need a measured asset/layout review.
+
+## Existing atmosphere to retain
+
+A cup has left a pale ring on Silas’s writing desk. Beyond the domestic rooms, a utility door leads toward the count chamber. Three photographs show the same study as its window is bricked, its cabinet moved and its bell painted. The ordinary changes hide an ordinary safe.
+
+This paragraph is archival narrative context, not a required arrival popup in the target design. Deliver its essential facts through the encounter actions; retain full writing in the optional journal.
+
+## Existing safe retreat
+
+You move into the utility vestibule and secure its mechanical bolt.
+
+## Encounter specifications
+
+- [PH-01 — Open the Mechanical Safe](open-the-mechanical-safe.md) — puzzle; required.
+- [PH-02 — Expose the Descent Entrance](expose-the-descent-entrance.md) — puzzle; required.
+- [PH-03 — Examine the Hidden Photograph](examine-the-hidden-photograph.md) — investigation; optional.
